1. Vowel Recognition dataset

Distributed dataset:
  - vowel (data/vowel.rda)

Source:
  UCI Machine Learning Repository, Vowel Recognition (Deterding Data).
  https://doi.org/10.24432/C58P4S

Original dataset creators:
  David Deterding, Mahesan Niranjan, and Tony Robinson.

Context-enriched version:
  The included data were prepared from vowel-context.data, which adds
  explicit speaker information, by Peter Turney. See Turney (1993),
  "Robust Classification With Context-Sensitive Features."

Use in this package:
  The dataset has 990 observations and 14 variables. The categorical
  codes for the training/test split, speaker, sex, and vowel class were
  converted to factors; the ten numeric acoustic features were retained
  without alteration.

